We use the `quickselect` function to find the k-th smallest element in the unsorted list. The `quickselect` function recursively partitions the array until the pivot element's index is equal to k. This allows us to find the median without fully sorting the array. 

By using the Quickselect algorithm, we reduce the time complexity of finding the median from O(n log n) to O(n). The mean calculation remains the same, with a time complexity of O(n).

